    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. **Added an `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 a static SLF4J logger named exactly `\"AUDIT\"`, matching the logger the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches to.\n\n2. **Emit the audit line after a successful create** \u2014 immediately after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`, so it only fires when creation succeeds (all validation/quota checks have passed and the owner has a generated id):\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line carries the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`, all of which `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` asserts are present in a single AUDIT event. The observed log confirms the format, e.g. `AUDIT - owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-01`.\n\nThe full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).",
