        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a minimal, additive fit for this file's existing structure:\n\n- The `AUDIT` logger is declared as a `private static final` field via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` \u2014 the standard slf4j idiom for a named logger, placed at the top of the class where a maintainer expects class constants.\n- The audit call sits immediately after `this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` on line 147\u2013149, i.e. exactly at the \"successful create\" point and after `id`/`customerCode`/`registrationDate` have all been assigned, so it reads the right values from the right place.\n- It uses parameterized logging (`{}` placeholders) rather than string concatenation, which is the idiomatic slf4j form.\n- Nothing is duplicated, and it doesn't turn any method into a catch-all \u2014 the `addOwner` handler already owns the full create flow (normalization, limit checks, code assignment, save), so emitting the create audit event alongside the save is consistent with how this controller is already organized. A maintainer of this file would find it natural."
